/nibs
.nibs/
# ...except the test fixture, which is a store on purpose. The layout inversion
# moved it from .nibs/*.md to .nibs/data/*.md, a path the rule above matches, so
# the 89 nibs stopped being tracked and a fresh checkout failed internal/reprefix
# on a fixture nothing regenerates. Negating the directory is what lets git
# descend: a rule excluding a DIRECTORY stops the walk, so re-including only the
# files beneath it cannot work.
!/testdata/fixtures/sample-project/.nibs/
